title: Mika renders the half-built S1.0 board under the CSP and finds a refusal the probe missed
summary: 'The Atelier UI gate flagged Kit''s in-progress build script. Instead of a waiver, Mika rendered Kit''s board bundle in headless Chrome under the verbatim CSP and found a CSP refusal in Excalidraw''s stock Library sidebar, a serif font fallback, and two loader defects. Verdict: approved-with-fixes, scoped to an unreachable engine fixture.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#gui-board'
  - '#doodle-mod'
learnings:
  - A waiver written by the orchestrator for its own builder's change is self-review; let the independent reviewer decide what is visual
  - Build scripts that rewrite a third-party engine's styles, fonts and images are visual in effect even though they live in scripts/
  - CSP probes must walk the engine's secondary UI (sidebars, dialogs, exporters), not only load, draw and export
  - UI gate reviews must name screenshots by absolute path
verification:
  status: partial
  details:
    note: Chrome only, on the 22:29 build; fixes sent to Kit, not yet confirmed landed
