  - T-2026-11-24-001
body: |-
  How it came about: the Stop hook's UI gate flagged packages/gnomon-gui/scripts/board-patches.mjs. The orchestrator tried to write a waiver ("build script, not visual"); the permission classifier refused that as undermining oversight. Mika then judged for herself: the script IS visual in effect, since four of its patches change what is drawn.

  Findings (rendered unless noted):
  - Select an element, press Library: style-src-attr and style-src-elem violations, because the sidebar writes an exported SVG preview with innerHTML. Thirteen other interactions were clean. This breaks S1.0's zero-refusals bar; the P12 probe did not walk this path.
  - The font-registry-empty patch leaves board text and PNG export in the UA default serif, measured differently per OS. S1.1 registers a bundled face.
  - The board bytes are embedded in the kernel's GUI bundle and served, but nothing mounts them; nothing enforced that yet. The isolation test must prove app.js cannot reach the chunk before the reskin.
  - By reading: loadBoard can mount before its stylesheet applies and never retries a failed stylesheet (core/board.ts:70-86); mountBoard cannot report a crash after mount (board/index.ts:33-37).
  - A 560px host flips the engine to its phone layout; S1.1 needs a minimum pane width.

  The gate then rejected her review once on form: the Rendered section must name screenshots by paths that exist on disk (relative names resolve against the repo root).
